============================== Start [case_context_per_thread,(),{}]
    2 threads, one context each: both outputs match the single-threaded reference
    Sharing one context across these threads is what the TensorRT API forbids -- the
    scratch space inside a context belongs to one inference in flight, not to a pool
============================== End   [case_context_per_thread]
============================== Start [case_graph_replays_addresses,(),{}]
    Overwriting the captured host buffer changes the result: the graph reads addresses
    Rebinding the context after capture leaves the graph untouched: it still writes to
    the old buffer, which is why a captured graph must own its buffers for its lifetime
============================== End   [case_graph_replays_addresses]
